Helios vkd3d-proton fork: inline producer signal, admission timing, GPU timestamps, ECL fence for presents

Conduit Basemark D3D12 on NVK. Applied after 0005.

- The Helios producer signal of an ExecuteCommandLists rides on the batch's
  own last vkQueueSubmit2 (one more VkSemaphoreSubmitInfo) instead of a
  separate submit, when that submit goes to this queue (a fallback-queue tail
  keeps the separate, joining submit). One NVK submit (a semaphore release
  with wait-for-idle and a non-stall interrupt) less per batch.
  HELIOS_VKD3D_INLINE_SIGNAL=0 turns it off.
- The worker records when each batch's admission event is seen: commit-to-
  admission and (ECL fences) admission-to-signal timing, plus inline vs
  separate producer signal counts, appended to helios_vkd3d_ecl_fence_stats.
- HELIOS_VKD3D_GPU_TIMESTAMPS=1 (off by default): a TOP_OF_PIPE timestamp in
  a submit right before each Helios batch and an ALL_COMMANDS one right after
  it, in a per-queue ring of 64 query pairs read back without waiting when a
  slot comes round. helios_vkd3d_gpu_time_stats: batches, GPU busy per batch
  (end - max(begin, previous end)), idle gap before each batch, maximum, and
  histograms. Two extra submits per batch while on.
- helios_vkd3d_create_ecl_fence(queue, value, &fence): another RM fence for a
  value of the queue's ECL timeline, for a scanout present that flips when
  the frame's last batch is done.
- helios_vkd3d.def exports the new entry points.

